const footerHtml = "Cambridge IGCSE Islamiyat 0493 &middot; Paper 1, Topic 2, Unit 2.2";
const mainHtml = "<section class=\"chapter\">\r\n      <div class=\"wrap\">\r\n        <div class=\"chapter-head\">\r\n          <h1>Compilation under Abu Bakr</h1>\r\n          <p class=\"ch-sub\">2.2 The Compilation under the Khalifas &middot; 12 AH &middot; the first mus-haf</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p class=\"lede prose-col\">Within a year of the Prophet's death, the new Muslim state faced a crisis that turned preservation from a background practice into an urgent project.</p>\r\n\r\n        <p class=\"prose-col\">Several Arab tribes rebelled against Madinah and rallied around a rival claimant to prophethood, <strong>Musaylimah</strong>. Caliph Abu Bakr sent an army to confront him at the <strong>Battle of Yamama</strong> (12 AH / 633 CE). The rebellion was crushed &mdash; but a large number of the Qur&rsquo;an's huffaz, reportedly around seventy, were among the Muslim dead.</p>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"steps\">\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">1</span>\r\n            <div><h4>&rsquo;Umar raises the alarm</h4><p>&rsquo;Umar ibn al-Khattab went to Abu Bakr, warning that if huffaz kept dying in battle at this rate across further campaigns, portions of the Qur&rsquo;an itself could be lost forever unless it was gathered into one authoritative written copy.</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">2</span>\r\n            <div><h4>Abu Bakr hesitates, then agrees</h4><p>His first response was caution: &ldquo;How can I do something the Messenger of Allah did not do?&rdquo; &rsquo;Umar kept pressing until, by Abu Bakr's own account, &ldquo;Allah opened my chest for that which He had opened the chest of &rsquo;Umar.&rdquo;</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">3</span>\r\n            <div><h4>Zayd ibn Thabit is chosen &mdash; and hesitates too</h4><p>Abu Bakr summoned Zayd, by then a respected scribe who had personally heard the Prophet's own final recitation. Zayd's first reaction mirrored Abu Bakr's own: he called it a task heavier than moving a mountain. He accepted on the same reasoning &mdash; that refusing to safeguard the Qur&rsquo;an would be the greater risk.</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">4</span>\r\n            <div><h4>A rigorous method, not a shortcut</h4><p>Zayd did not simply write from his own memory. He collected the Qur&rsquo;an &ldquo;from date-palm stalks, thin white stones, and the hearts of men,&rdquo; accepting each verse only where it was independently confirmed &mdash; matched against both a written record from the Prophet's own lifetime <em>and</em> corroborating testimony that it had been heard directly from the Prophet.</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div class=\"step\">\r\n            <span class=\"n\">5</span>\r\n            <div><h4>One finished mus-haf</h4><p>The completed single volume &mdash; called a <em>mus-haf</em> &mdash; was kept with Abu Bakr, then passed to &rsquo;Umar when he became Caliph, and on &rsquo;Umar's death passed to his daughter <strong>Hafsa bint &rsquo;Umar</strong>, one of the Prophet's widows, for safekeeping. It would matter again within twenty years.</p></div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div style=\"max-width:66ch; margin:40px auto 0;\" class=\"prose-col\">\r\n          <h3 style=\"display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap;\">Ready to practise?</h3>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-top:10px; color:var(--ink-soft);\">A short Practice Quiz first, then a graded Quiz once you're confident.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"lesson-pager\">\r\n          <a class=\"pager-link\" href=\"../preservation-before-compilation/quiz.html\"><span class=\"pg-label\">&larr; Back</span><div class=\"pg-title\">Preservation Before Compilation Quiz</div></a>\r\n          <a class=\"pager-link next\" href=\"practice.html\"><span class=\"pg-label\">Next &rarr;</span><div class=\"pg-title\">Practice Quiz</div></a>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>";
